\v 9 \wj Whether is it easier to say to the sick of the palsy, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and take up thy bed, and walk?\wj* 
\v 10 \wj But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins,\wj* ([he saith]{strong=“G3004” x-morph=“robinson: V-\sc Pai\sc*-3S 16”} [to the sick of the palsy]{strong=“G3885” x-morph=“robinson: A-\sc Dsm\sc* 18”},) 
\v 11 \wj I say unto thee, Arise, and take up thy bed, and go thy way into thine house.\wj* 
